---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import Terminal from '../components/Terminal.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/pages/PageHead.astro';
import PageFoot from '../components/pages/PageFoot.astro';
import BoxDiagram from '../components/pages/BoxDiagram.astro';
import Ledger from '../components/pages/Ledger.astro';

const docs = [
  { href: '/docs/remote/', label: 'Remote boxes' },
  { href: '/docs/guides/remote-setup/', label: 'Preparing a box' },
  { href: '/docs/guides/remote-command/', label: 'Boxes reached by a command' },
  { href: '/docs/guides/remote-multiple-boxes/', label: 'Several boxes with the same project' },
  { href: '/docs/security/', label: 'Security' }
];

const ledger = [
  {
    title: 'The usual way',
    items: [
      {
        code: 'http://10.0.3.14:20011',
        text: 'A private IP in the address bar. Cookies, CORS and OAuth callbacks wanted a hostname.'
      },
      {
        code: 'ssh -L 20011:localhost:20011 my-vps',
        text: 'One forward per port, typed again after every sleep.'
      },
      {
        code: '*.dev.example.com, a wildcard cert, a subdomain per branch',
        text: 'DNS, certbot and a proxy config, for a sandbox that lives an hour.'
      },
      {
        code: 'https://random-words.example.dev',
        text: 'A public URL for something that was never meant to leave the machine.'
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    title: 'With devlanes',
    items: [
      {
        code: 'devlanes remote connect my-vps --background',
        text: 'One command. The connection belongs to your local daemon and stays until you disconnect.'
      },
      {
        code: 'https://myapp1.localhost',
        text: "The box's hostnames join your local proxy, with your local certificate."
      },
      {
        code: 'psql -h 127.0.0.1 -p 20013 myapp_lane1',
        text: "Databases, debuggers, gRPC and websockets, on the box's own port numbers."
      },
      {
        code: 'devlanes daemon pair',
        text: 'A one-time code pairs your machine. The box keeps a hash of the token.'
      }
    ]
  }
];
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Remote boxes"
  description="Run the lanes on a VPS, a container or a codespace and open them from your laptop. devlanes mirrors the box's hostnames and ports over one ssh session; the box opens no ports."
  path="/remote/"
  current="remote"
>
  <PageHead title="The lanes run on a box. Your laptop gets their hostnames and ports.">
    <p>
      A box is any machine that runs devlanes and that you can reach with <code>ssh</code>, or with
      a command such as <code>docker exec</code>. Your laptop's daemon mirrors the box's lanes over
      one session, with the same names and the same port numbers, and the box opens no ports.
    </p>
  </PageHead>

  <Section
    id="ledger"
    title="Nobody sets up DNS and a wildcard cert for an hour-long sandbox."
    stacked
  >
    <p>
      A dev server on a box was always reachable somehow: a private IP, a forward per port, a public
      tunnel. None of it is worth doing for a lane an agent will throw away before lunch, so it did
      not get done. With devlanes the box's lanes show up on your laptop by default.
    </p>
    <Ledger slot="visual" columns={ledger} />
  </Section>

  <Section id="pair" title="Pair once. The box opens no ports.">
    <p>
      The box prints a code that works once and expires in 10 minutes. Your laptop trades it for a
      token the box keeps only a hash of. From then on the connection belongs to your local daemon:
      it survives sleep, network loss and restarts, until you disconnect.
    </p>
    <p>
      Anything you can reach over ssh can be a box. The tunnel runs inside the session itself, so
      the box needs no TCP forwarding enabled and no firewall rule.
    </p>
    <div slot="visual" class="terminal-stack">
      <Terminal title="on my-vps">
        <pre class="terminal-content"><span class="command">$ devlanes daemon pair</span>
pairing code: <span class="url">K7QM-3XWD</span>
it works once and expires in 10 minutes
on your other machine, run:
  devlanes remote connect &lt;box&gt; --code K7QM-3XWD</pre>
      </Terminal>
      <Terminal title="on your laptop">
        <pre class="terminal-content terminal-scroll"><span class="command">$ devlanes remote connect my-vps --code K7QM-3XWD --background</span>
<span class="command">$ devlanes url ls</span>
HOST                      TARGET       PORT   STATE
api.myapp1.localhost  ->  myapp@1:api  20010  <span class="success">ready</span>
myapp1.localhost      ->  myapp@1:web  20011  <span class="success">ready</span></pre>
      </Terminal>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section id="mirror" title="Same ports, same hostnames, on your laptop." stacked>
    <p>
      Your laptop binds the box's port numbers on its own 127.0.0.1 and adds the box's hostnames to
      your proxy, with the certificate you already trust. The URL a service prints on the box is the
      one you open here, and <code>psql</code>, a debugger, gRPC or websockets connect as if the
      service were local.
    </p>
    <BoxDiagram slot="visual" />
  </Section>

  <Section id="tui" title="The box's lane shows up in your TUI.">
    <p>
      A connected box's lanes join the project tab after your own, with their domain, their ports
      and the URL that opens each one on this machine. Starting and stopping stays on the box; the
      pane says what to run there.
    </p>
    <Terminal slot="visual" title="devlanes, lane @1 on my-vps">
      <pre class="terminal-content terminal-scroll tui-text"><span class="url">devlanes</span>  <span class="dim">1 myapp</span>         <span class="dim">Monitor  Daemon  Boxes</span>
<span class="dim">lanes</span>  <span class="dim">1 @0 main</span>  <span class="tui-selected"> 2 @1 my-vps </span> <span class="dim">[ ] switch lanes</span>
<span class="dim">┌</span> myapp@1  running · 3 up <span class="dim">──────────</span> <span class="url">on my-vps</span> <span class="dim">┐</span>
<span class="dim">│</span> <span class="dim">box</span>       my-vps · ssh · devlanes 0.10.0     <span class="dim">│</span>
<span class="dim">│</span> <span class="dim">domain</span>    myapp1.localhost                   <span class="dim">│</span>
<span class="dim">│</span> <span class="dim">services</span>  3 of 3 up                          <span class="dim">│</span>
<span class="dim">│</span> <span class="dim">infra</span>     postgres :20013                    <span class="dim">│</span>
<span class="dim">│</span> <span class="dim">ports</span>     4 of 4 mirrored here               <span class="dim">│</span>
<span class="dim">│</span> <span class="dim">urls</span>      <span class="url">https://api.myapp1.localhost</span>       <span class="dim">│</span>
<span class="dim">│</span>           <span class="url">https://myapp1.localhost</span>           <span class="dim">│</span>
<span class="dim">│</span>                                              <span class="dim">│</span>
<span class="dim">│</span> <span class="dim">Read-only here. On my-vps: ssh my-vps,</span>       <span class="dim">│</span>
<span class="dim">│</span> <span class="dim">then devlanes status myapp@1</span>                 <span class="dim">│</span>
<span class="dim">└──────────────────────────────────────────────┘</span>
 o <span class="dim">open in browser</span>   [ ] <span class="dim">switch lane</span>   ? <span class="dim">all keys</span></pre>
    </Terminal>
  </Section>

  <Section id="command" title="No ssh on the box? A command works too." reverse>
    <p>
      A container, a pod, a WSL distribution or a codespace has no sshd, but each has a command that
      runs a program inside it: <code>docker exec</code>, <code>kubectl exec</code>,{' '}
      <code>wsl.exe</code>, <code>gh codespace ssh</code>. Name the box in your user config with
      that command and it connects and pairs like any ssh host.
    </p>
    <Terminal slot="visual" title="~/.devlanes/config.yaml">
      <pre class="terminal-content"><span class="key">remote</span>:
  <span class="key">boxes</span>:
    <span class="key">myapp</span>:
      <span class="key">command</span>:
        - docker
        - exec
        - -i
        - myapp
        - devlanes
        - tunnel
        - --stdio</pre>
    </Terminal>
  </Section>

  <PageFoot links={docs} />
</SiteLayout>
